{"obsah":"<p>This weekend, and Friday too, was a bit more demanding. Getting used to the coaching pace and organising events after Covid is tough, but the results are worth it. On Friday and Saturday Vlasta had individual coaching in Tehov, while Mára, Lukáš and Katarína with Matouš taught skill-hungry women and girls on the Šembera trails. In the individual courses the main goal was learning to jump benches. Surprisingly, everyone who came – even though it didn't look like it at first – fought hard and sent the benches at full commitment.  </p>\n\n<p>So far we've also collected positive reactions about the camp. The Šembera trails are aimed more at families and kids, but you can still find a few things there where a rider can learn something and fine-tune their style. Some riders found the trail profile just right for them, while others would deserve harder, more demanding sections.</p>\n\n<p>You keep bombarding us with interest in a camp during or after the summer holidays. We'll try to prepare a few dates, but given our Trial exhibitions it will take some time. It should be clear in the first week of July :)<br><br>Next weekend, \"btw\", you can see us at <a href=\"http://www.vsenakolech.cz/\">www.vsenakolech.cz</a> in Kostelec or in Prostřední Bečva in Moravia.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped\"><ul class=\"blocks-gallery-grid\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F06%2F20210612_090337-scaled.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F06%2F20210612_090337.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"192418\" data-full-url=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F06%2F20210612_090337-scaled.webp?alt=media\" data-link=\"https://bikeskills.cz/?attachment_id=